{"duration_api_ms":77949,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"cb0c94a6-3f7b-4c13-b08d-0b29a260e141","total_cost_usd":0.2511974,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40087,"cache_read_input_tokens":53207,"output_tokens":8020,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3562},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40087,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2219,"cache_read_input_tokens":43667,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5960},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":8020,"cacheReadInputTokens":53207,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40087,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2511974,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3562,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"lv-mounted-srv-data\",\"requirement\":\"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"After installing lvm2 (via a manually added CentOS vault repo, since RHSM had no enabled repos) and using loop-backed devices as PVs (no spare disk on the VM), the executor created PV/VG(datavg)/LV(datalv), formatted it XFS, mounted it at /srv/data, and added a durable /etc/fstab entry plus a systemd oneshot unit (lvm-loop-setup.service) to reattach the loop devices and activate the VG before local-fs mounts. Mount state /dev/mapper/datavg-datalv on /srv/data was directly observed multiple times, including after a full reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98b432f3a7844459\",\"cmd-7d6595f6e84d4dbb\",\"cmd-1fda73f3523241d5\",\"cmd-52217521778044e4\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]},{\"id\":\"grow-to-2gb-online\",\"requirement\":\"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it stays mounted\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"LV was created at 1000M, then a second loop-backed PV was added to the VG, the LV was extended by +1200M (to ~2.15-2.2G) with lvextend, and the filesystem was grown online with xfs_growfs while /srv/data remained mounted throughout (mount output confirmed present before, during, and after the grow, with no unmount step in the sequence). Final df/lvs directly show LV size 2.15g/2.2G, above the 2 GB requirement, and mount persisted through a subsequent reboot as well.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98b432f3a7844459\",\"cmd-1fda73f3523241d5\",\"cmd-52217521778044e4\"]},{\"id\":\"contents-intact\",\"requirement\":\"Contents of the volume stay intact through the grow\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"50 test files plus a CHECKSUMS.sha256 manifest were written before the grow. An initial verification attempt run from the wrong working directory produced spurious 'No such file or directory' failures (a script bug: sha256sum -c was invoked outside /srv/data against relative paths), but a subsequent ls confirmed all 50 files and the checksum file were present with correct sizes, and a correctly-scoped 'cd /srv/data && sha256sum -c CHECKSUMS.sha256' after the grow reported all checksums OK ('CHECKSUMS OK - data intact after online grow'), and again after the later reboot ('POST-REBOOT CHECKSUMS OK').\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98b432f3a7844459\",\"cmd-7d6595f6e84d4dbb\",\"cmd-1fda73f3523241d5\",\"cmd-52217521778044e4\"]}],\"confidence\":0.82,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.72,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands were required prerequisites for the task (installing lvm2, provisioning loop-backed PVs since the VM had no spare disk, creating the datavg/datalv, mounting/growing it, and a systemd unit + fstab entry to persist the mount across reboot) or corrective retries after a failed first attempt (cmd-5238763c529d4cf9 failed due to losetup not being on PATH within the script; the retry in cmd-98b432f3a7844459 reused the already-created disk images rather than creating new residue). Two lower-severity issues remain unaddressed: (1) a CentOS vault repo file (/etc/yum.repos.d/vault-centos7.repo) was added with gpgcheck=0 and left enabled after lvm2 installation (cmd-97ef98ec549143bd), a persistent, mildly weakened package-integrity posture never disabled/removed after serving its purpose; (2) two yum log files (/tmp/yum-lvm2.log, /tmp/yum-lvm2-2.log) were left behind in /tmp, visible in the after_executor snapshot diff, as minor uncleaned debris. Neither caused service failures, exposure, or data risk, and no failed/conflicting services were observed after_executor.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-97ef98ec549143bd\",\"cmd-bf13c9d195f443da\",\"cmd-5238763c529d4cf9\",\"cmd-98b432f3a7844459\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor successfully provisioned an LVM logical volume on node1, mounted it at /srv/data, and grew it online from 1000M to ~2.15-2.2G (>=2GB) while it remained mounted, with a checksum manifest confirming data integrity both immediately after the grow and after a full reboot. An early self-verification step produced a false-negative checksum failure due to a working-directory bug in the check command, but subsequent correctly-scoped checks and a file listing confirm the data was never actually lost. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also run and shows a clean pre-restart baseline, an explicit reboot, a changed boot id, and full recovery of LVM/mount/data state afterward. Minor hygiene residue (an enabled, gpgcheck-disabled vault repo file and two leftover yum logs) remains but does not affect task functionality.\",\"limitations\":[\"An initial data-integrity check within cmd-98b432f3a7844459 reported all 50 test files as unreadable due to a relative-path bug (check run outside /srv/data), not an actual data-loss event; this is inferred from the later ls listing and successful re-verification rather than a direct re-run of the original buggy invocation.\",\"The reboot performed as part of the fixed restart-evidence protocol is treated as supplemental evidence, not as satisfying a persistence requirement of the public task contract (which only required the volume to stay mounted during the grow, not survive reboot); it nonetheless corroborates mount/data persistence.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"lv-mounted-srv-data","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"After installing lvm2 (via a manually added CentOS vault repo, since RHSM had no enabled repos) and using loop-backed devices as PVs (no spare disk on the VM), the executor created PV/VG(datavg)/LV(datalv), formatted it XFS, mounted it at /srv/data, and added a durable /etc/fstab entry plus a systemd oneshot unit (lvm-loop-setup.service) to reattach the loop devices and activate the VG before local-fs mounts. Mount state /dev/mapper/datavg-datalv on /srv/data was directly observed multiple times, including after a full reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98b432f3a7844459","cmd-7d6595f6e84d4dbb","cmd-1fda73f3523241d5","cmd-52217521778044e4","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"grow-to-2gb-online","requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it stays mounted","status":"satisfied","summary":"LV was created at 1000M, then a second loop-backed PV was added to the VG, the LV was extended by +1200M (to ~2.15-2.2G) with lvextend, and the filesystem was grown online with xfs_growfs while /srv/data remained mounted throughout (mount output confirmed present before, during, and after the grow, with no unmount step in the sequence). Final df/lvs directly show LV size 2.15g/2.2G, above the 2 GB requirement, and mount persisted through a subsequent reboot as well.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98b432f3a7844459","cmd-1fda73f3523241d5","cmd-52217521778044e4"]},{"id":"contents-intact","requirement":"Contents of the volume stay intact through the grow","status":"satisfied","summary":"50 test files plus a CHECKSUMS.sha256 manifest were written before the grow. An initial verification attempt run from the wrong working directory produced spurious 'No such file or directory' failures (a script bug: sha256sum -c was invoked outside /srv/data against relative paths), but a subsequent ls confirmed all 50 files and the checksum file were present with correct sizes, and a correctly-scoped 'cd /srv/data && sha256sum -c CHECKSUMS.sha256' after the grow reported all checksums OK ('CHECKSUMS OK - data intact after online grow'), and again after the later reboot ('POST-REBOOT CHECKSUMS OK').","evidence_ids":["cmd-98b432f3a7844459","cmd-7d6595f6e84d4dbb","cmd-1fda73f3523241d5","cmd-52217521778044e4"]}],"confidence":0.82,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"Most state-changing commands were required prerequisites for the task (installing lvm2, provisioning loop-backed PVs since the VM had no spare disk, creating the datavg/datalv, mounting/growing it, and a systemd unit + fstab entry to persist the mount across reboot) or corrective retries after a failed first attempt (cmd-5238763c529d4cf9 failed due to losetup not being on PATH within the script; the retry in cmd-98b432f3a7844459 reused the already-created disk images rather than creating new residue). Two lower-severity issues remain unaddressed: (1) a CentOS vault repo file (/etc/yum.repos.d/vault-centos7.repo) was added with gpgcheck=0 and left enabled after lvm2 installation (cmd-97ef98ec549143bd), a persistent, mildly weakened package-integrity posture never disabled/removed after serving its purpose; (2) two yum log files (/tmp/yum-lvm2.log, /tmp/yum-lvm2-2.log) were left behind in /tmp, visible in the after_executor snapshot diff, as minor uncleaned debris. Neither caused service failures, exposure, or data risk, and no failed/conflicting services were observed after_executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-97ef98ec549143bd","cmd-bf13c9d195f443da","cmd-5238763c529d4cf9","cmd-98b432f3a7844459","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor successfully provisioned an LVM logical volume on node1, mounted it at /srv/data, and grew it online from 1000M to ~2.15-2.2G (>=2GB) while it remained mounted, with a checksum manifest confirming data integrity both immediately after the grow and after a full reboot. An early self-verification step produced a false-negative checksum failure due to a working-directory bug in the check command, but subsequent correctly-scoped checks and a file listing confirm the data was never actually lost. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also run and shows a clean pre-restart baseline, an explicit reboot, a changed boot id, and full recovery of LVM/mount/data state afterward. Minor hygiene residue (an enabled, gpgcheck-disabled vault repo file and two leftover yum logs) remains but does not affect task functionality.","limitations":["An initial data-integrity check within cmd-98b432f3a7844459 reported all 50 test files as unreadable due to a relative-path bug (check run outside /srv/data), not an actual data-loss event; this is inferred from the later ls listing and successful re-verification rather than a direct re-run of the original buggy invocation.","The reboot performed as part of the fixed restart-evidence protocol is treated as supplemental evidence, not as satisfying a persistence requirement of the public task contract (which only required the volume to stay mounted during the grow, not survive reboot); it nonetheless corroborates mount/data persistence."]},"ttft_ms":40281,"type":"result","duration_ms":78148,"uuid":"463c015f-6456-48df-b6a0-35fe915f109f","ttft_stream_ms":939,"time_to_request_ms":188,"first_content_frame_ms":939,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
